# Glyph Coverage

This one-page fixture checks core text encoding, semantic checkboxes, and deterministic missing-glyph diagnostics across DOCX, PDF, and PNG.

## Core Encoding Baseline

ASCII: The quick brown fox jumps over 13 lazy dogs.

CP1252: café, “double quotes”, ‘single quotes’, em dash —, and euro €.

## Semantic Checkboxes

#paragraph[
Explicit controls: #checkbox(checked = true, name = "approved", title = "Approved") checked and #checkbox(checked = false, name = "pending", title = "Pending") unchecked.
]

- [x] Checked markdown task item.
- [ ] Unchecked markdown task item.

## Missing Glyph Diagnostic

The literal checked-box glyph between these ASCII brackets is the deliberate coverage failure: [☑].

DOCX should preserve it without a Mote warning. PDF and PNG should each draw one visible question-mark fallback and emit exactly one missing-glyph diagnostic.
